279,7015,438,1181,14887,11,1128,374,279,8028,6785,1372,315,2849,1573,807,525,678,304,279,4734,1852,10468,1549,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nPlanets X, Y and Z take 360, 450 and 540 days, respectively, to rotate around the same sun. If the three planets are lined up in a ray having the sun as its endpoint, what is the minimum positive number of days before they are all in the exact same locations again?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"84c60b0de097ebe33677302018dc6d68ba39f484b0f80d061b84f338e36d4ff4"},"seconds":9.64962100982666,"seed":487520757056880222,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the minimum positive number of days before planets X, Y, and Z are all in the exact same locations again, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their orbital periods. The orbital periods are 360 days for planet X, 450 days for planet Y, and 540 days for planet Z.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of each number:\n- The prime factorization of 360 is:\n  \\[\n  360 = 2^3 \\times 3^2 \\times 5\n  \\]\n- The prime factorization of 450 is:\n  \\[\n  450 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5^2\n  \\]\n- The prime factorization of 540 is:\n  \\[\n  540 = 2^2 \\times 3^3 \\times 5\n  \\]\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime number that appears in the factorizations:\n- The highest power of 2 is \\(2^3\\).\n- The highest power of 3 is \\(3^3\\).\n- The highest power of 5 is \\(5^2\\).\n\nTherefore, the LCM is:\n\\[\nLCM = 2^3 \\times 3^3 \\times 5^2 = 8 \\times 27 \\times 25\n\\]\n\nWe can calculate this step-by-step:\n\\[\n8 \\times 27 = 216\n\\]\n\\[\n216 \\times 25 = 5400\n\\]\n\nThus, the minimum positive number of days before planets X, Y, and Z are all in the exact same locations again is \\(\\boxed{5400}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{5400}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:864"}
